const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文检验个券的流动性度量是否随共同市场条件而变化。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Commonality in Liquidity” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源把个券与市场汇总的价差、深度和交易活跃度放在同一横截面与时间序列框架中比较。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Commonality in Liquidity”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要可比较的报价价差、深度、成交量、个券权重、市场汇总规则及交易日时间对齐。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Commonality in Liquidity”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"研究关注流动性共同变化，而不是声称任一单一指标即可完整代表交易成本或市场承压。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Commonality in Liquidity”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"统一报价、深度和成交字段口径，保留样本成员变动与停牌，明确市场汇总权重及异常行情处理。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Commonality in Liquidity”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Financial Economics (2000)。不同交易制度下的价差和深度不必可比；日频代理也不能取代原文所需的报价和订单簿观察。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Financial Economics (2000) for “Commonality in Liquidity”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Commonality in Liquidity”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。不同交易制度下的价差和深度不必可比；日频代理也不能取代原文所需的报价和订单簿观察。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Commonality in Liquidity”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
